            Episode 1: <m>C</m> = <q>there are more variables than equations</q>,
            <m>J</m> = <q>there will be a free variable</q>; <m>c^1 = 1</m>;
            <m>c^2 = 1</m>, because more columns than rows forces a non-pivot column
            regardless of consistency. Episode 2 (<c>relation = chained(1)</c>):
            <m>C</m> = <q>there will be a free variable</q>, <m>J</m> = <q>it can't
            have exactly one solution</q>, scored exactly as STU-A. Record both rows
